    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## What I did\n\nUnified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit`.\n\n**`OwnerDerivations.java`**\n- Replaced `customerCode(...)` and `membershipNumber(...)` with `memberId(region, telephone, lastName, registrationDate)`, which builds `base = region + fiscalYearSegment + hash8` and appends `checkDigit(base)` \u2014 a single Luhn digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`. The existing `hash8`, `checkDigit` (Luhn), and `fiscalYearSegment` helpers are reused unchanged.\n- Rewrote the region read-back: `memberIdRegion` now parses the leading run of letters (the region precedes the 2-digit FY), replacing the old `-`-delimited `customerCodeRegion`. `locality(...)` now takes the `memberId`.\n\n**`Owner.java`** \u2014 Dropped the `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` persistent fields plus their accessors, dropped the transient `getCheckDigit()`, added a persistent `memberId` field with accessors, replaced `computeCustomerCode`/`computeMembershipNumber` with `computeMemberId`, and pointed `getLocality()` at `memberId`.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 `deduplicatedCustomerCode` \u2192 `deduplicatedMemberId` (collision handling now applies to the `memberId`, appending `-<n>`); `assignDerivedAttributes` sets `memberId` and no longer sets a membership number.\n\n**`OwnerCreationAuditor.java`** \u2014 Both the human-readable line and the structured `OWNER_CREATED` JSON event now carry `memberId` instead of `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, and `membershipNumber` schema properties with a single `memberId` (the generated `OwnerDto` and MapStruct mapping follow automatically), and updated the `locality` description.\n\n**DB schemas** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Replaced `customer_code` with `member_id VARCHAR(40)` and removed `membership_number`.\n\nThe owner segment (via `locality`), the fiscal-year segment, and the audit record all now derive from / reference the unified `memberId`, e.g. `NSW2716E6609E1` = `NSW` + `27` + `16E6609E` + Luhn `1`.",
